title: Prefabs changed outside Griff
intro: Each copy of a prefab remembers the version it was made from. When the prefab's file changes outside Griff, after a pull, in a text editor or by an agent, its copies follow, keeping their own changes.
project: Platformer | Prefab Versions

chapter: A prefab and its copies | Entity > Save as Prefab
look: 8, -2, 4
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Gem
set: Transform.Position = 5, -3, 0
set: Sprite.Tint = #29ADFF
set: Sprite.Size = 0.6, 0.6
add: Pickup
menu: Entity > Save as Prefab
expectfile: Prefabs/Gem.prefab
key: Ctrl+D
rename: Gem 2
set: Transform.Position = 7.5, -3, 0
set: Pickup.Amount = 5
expectprefab: Gem 2 = Gem
say: Here's a gem prefab and two copies of it. The second is worth five points: a change of its own.

chapter: The file changes on disk | A pull, a text editor or an agent
write: Prefabs/Gem.prefab | prefab-versions/Gem.prefab
wait: 2
say: Now the prefab's file changes outside Griff: a teammate's new version comes in with a pull, and gems are orange.
wait: 4
expectvalue: Gem.Sprite.Tint = #FFA300
expectvalue: Gem 2.Sprite.Tint = #FFA300
expectvalue: Gem 2.Pickup.Amount = 5
expectat: Gem 2 = 7.5, -3
explain: world:4, -1.5, 9.5, -4.2 | Copies follow the file | Griff notices the file changed and brings every copy up to date, here and in the other scenes. Each copy remembers the version it was made from, so the second gem keeps its five points and its place.
key: Ctrl+Z
expectvalue: Gem 2.Sprite.Tint = #29ADFF
say: In the open scene it's one step to undo, like saving the prefab here.
key: Ctrl+Y
expectvalue: Gem 2.Sprite.Tint = #FFA300
say: A prefab that changed while the project was closed catches up the same way as the project opens.
